//@version=5
// ============================================================================
//  AEOX Signal Confirm v1 (Free — Educational)
//
//  WHAT THIS TEACHES
//  "A signal isn't real 'til the candle closes."
//  On a live bar, Pine evaluates your conditions on EVERY tick. A condition
//  that is true at 14:32 can be false at 14:59 — the marker you saw mid-bar
//  simply vanishes at close. That is why indicators "look perfect after the
//  move but fall apart in live trading".
//
//  This script draws signals ONLY when the bar has closed and confirmed
//  (barstate.isconfirmed). The optional "ghost" markers show the raw,
//  unconfirmed signal on the live bar — turn them on and watch a ghost
//  appear, flicker and disappear before the close. That flicker IS repaint,
//  demonstrated on your own chart.
//
//  RULE USED (fixed, public teaching rule — same as the AEOX RSI-4 Primer):
//    BUY  : price above SMA(100) (uptrend) AND RSI(4) crosses under 10
//           → buying a dip inside an uptrend.
//    SELL : RSI(4) crosses over 70.
//  Thresholds 10 / 70 are fixed ON PURPOSE: this is a transparency teaching
//  tool, not a tuneable trading system.
//
//  ALERT GUIDE (see P3 in our research): the single alertcondition below only
//  fires when the bar has CONFIRMED. Even if you create the alert with
//  "Once per bar" instead of "Once per bar close", the barstate.isconfirmed
//  guard ensures it fires at the close — so alerts match what you see on the
//  chart, and match the strategy tester's bar-close model.
//
//  Educational tool, not financial advice.
//
//  LICENSE: free for personal use. No redistribution or resale.
//  (c) 2026 AEOX · quant.aeox.uk
// ============================================================================
indicator("AEOX Signal Confirm v1 (Free)", overlay=true)

// ---- classic parameters only (textbook-level inputs are allowed; the logic
//      itself stays fixed — that is the point of the free teaching line) ----
rsiLen = input.int(4,   "RSI length",  minval=1, group="Classic parameters")
smaLen = input.int(100, "Trend SMA length", minval=1, group="Classic parameters")

showGhost = input.bool(false, "Show provisional (unconfirmed) ghost signals",
     group="Teaching", tooltip="Ghost x-marks appear and disappear while the live bar is still open. They exist to DEMONSTRATE intrabar flicker. They will never match a confirmed BUY/SELL unless the bar closes with the condition still true.")

// Fixed thresholds — deliberately NOT inputs (free-line moat rule).
OS_LEVEL = 10
OB_LEVEL = 70

// ---- calculations (identical shape to the RSI-4 Primer rule) ----
rsi     = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
trendUp = close > ta.sma(close, smaLen)   // "should we be long-biased at all?"

// Raw conditions: these flicker on the live bar. On historical bars they are
// already final (historical bars only ever evaluate once, at their close).
buyRaw  = trendUp and ta.crossunder(rsi, OS_LEVEL)
sellRaw = ta.crossover(rsi, OB_LEVEL)

// Confirmed conditions: barstate.isconfirmed is TRUE only on the final tick
// of the live bar (and always true on historical bars). The shape below is
// therefore drawn only once the candle has actually closed.
buyConf  = buyRaw  and barstate.isconfirmed
sellConf = sellRaw and barstate.isconfirmed

// ---- plotting: confirmed signals are solid; ghosts are grey x-marks ----
plotshape(buyConf,  "BUY (confirmed)",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar,
     color.new(color.green, 0), size=size.small, text="BUY",  textcolor=color.green)
plotshape(sellConf, "SELL (confirmed)", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar,
     color.new(color.red, 0),   size=size.small, text="SELL", textcolor=color.red)

plotshape(showGhost and buyRaw  and not barstate.isconfirmed, "Provisional BUY (ghost)",
     shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.gray, 0), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showGhost and sellRaw and not barstate.isconfirmed, "Provisional SELL (ghost)",
     shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.gray, 0), size=size.tiny)

// ---- the single allowed alert: confirmed BUY only ----
// Create the alert on this condition; the isconfirmed guard makes the firing
// time unambiguous (bar close), no matter which "trigger frequency" you pick.
alertcondition(buyConf, "Confirmed BUY (fires on bar close)",
     "AEOX Signal Confirm: confirmed BUY {{ticker}} {{interval}} @ {{close}}")

// ============================================================================
//  WHEN THIS TOOL MISLEADS (know the limits of the demo)
//  - Confirmation removes intrabar flicker, but NOT lookahead bias: if you
//    back-test a rule and then "improve" it until the equity curve looks
//    good, you have curve-fitted, not confirmed.
//  - Confirmed signals are always LATE by construction — you trade
//    reliability for a fraction of the move. That trade-off is the lesson.
//  - This script has no stops, no position tracking, no sizing. It marks
//    educational events only. Risk engineering lives in the Premium Suite.
//
//  VERIFY IT YOURSELF
//  Compare these signals with the free web dashboard (independent
//  implementation, fee-inclusive honest backtests):
//    → quant.aeox.uk
//  More free resources (guides, primers, bundles):
//    → go.aeox.uk
//
//  Educational tool, not financial advice.
//  (c) 2026 AEOX · free for personal use, no redistribution or resale.
// ============================================================================
